<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Bonny Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1450 CE – 1884 CE (approx.) · capital Bonny</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Ijaw trading state of the eastern Niger delta, one of the busiest slave ports of the 18th century and then a centre of the palm oil trade.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Bonny, called Ibani by its people, was founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ijaw-people">Ijaw</a> migrants on an island near the mouth of the Bonny river, traditionally in the 15th century. By the 17th century it was dealing with Portuguese, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> and English ships, buying captives from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/igbo-people">Igbo</a> hinterland through networks such as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/aro-confederacy">Aro Confederacy</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amanyanabo">Amanyanabo</a> ruled with the heads of trading houses, which absorbed slaves and could be led by able former slaves. The Pepple dynasty, founded by Perekule in the 18th century, presided over a huge <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">slave trade</a> and then a shift to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palm-oil">palm oil</a> after abolition. The British consul deposed King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-dappa-pepple">William Dappa Pepple</a> in 1854.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1869 the former slave and house head <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaja-of-opobo">Jaja</a> left Bonny to found the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-opobo">Kingdom of Opobo</a>, taking much of its trade. Bonny signed a British protection treaty in 1884 and became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/oil-rivers-protectorate">Oil Rivers Protectorate</a>. It is now a key oil and gas terminal.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 1450 CE – 1884 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-